      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Documentation Principles",
      "anchor": "documentation-principles"
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Nodics documentation must be useful before it is clever."
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Every guide should answer:"
    },
    {
      "kind": "unordered-list",
      "items": [
        "What problem does this feature solve?",
        "When should I use it?",
        "Where should I make the change?",
        "What files or configuration are involved?",
        "What should I avoid?",
        "How do I verify that it works?",
        "How can a project customize this without changing Nodics framework code?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Avoid internal folder names in page titles unless the folder name is the thing the user must open. Prefer task names such as \"How to create a scheduled job\" instead of implementation names such as \"cronjob module\"."
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Relationship With Module Documentation",
      "anchor": "relationship-with-module-documentation"
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "This folder explains Nodics from the user and application-developer point of view."
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Module `README.md` files explain the details of one specific capability. For example, this documentation may say how scheduled jobs work in Nodics, while the scheduled-job module README explains the exact schemas, services, routes, and extension contracts owned by that module."
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Use the [Module Documentation Index](reference/module-documentation-index.md) to move from task-based guides to the module that owns the exact capability details."
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "AI-only and implementation-governance rules belong in `AGENTS.md` and `gSetup/llm`, not in public user documentation."
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Where To Find The Right Guidance",
